# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.log

# Secrets: never commit real values. Template lives in .env.example
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# AL AI runtime artifacts
.al-ai-bot.lock
# Bootstrapper state and service logs (scripts/dev.ps1): state, the running pids,
# and per-service stdout/stderr. Regenerated on every start; never a source of
# truth. Distinct from the database cluster at %USERPROFILE%\.al-ai\pgdata,
# which is deliberately outside the repository.
.al-ai/

# Database dumps. They are a point-in-time copy of live rows â€” including the
# encrypted OAuth tokens in `oauth_sessions` â€” and belong next to the data
# directory, not in history where they can never be removed.
.workbuddy-ai/backups/

# Generated screen previews (bundled JS + CSS + the throwaway generators that
# build them). Regenerate on demand; never a source of truth.
.workbuddy-ai/preview/

# Screenshots written by the browser verification harness
# (`.workbuddy-ai/verify/browser-check.mjs`). The harness itself is source and
# stays tracked; its output is regenerated on every run.
.workbuddy-ai/verify/*.png

# Local convenience links: on this machine .claude/skills and
# .zcode/skills are directory junctions onto .agents/skills. Git cannot
# track a junction as a link, so committing them would add two more copies of
# the same twenty-one files. The canonical set lives in .agents/skills.
.claude/skills/
.zcode/skills/
